    "knowledge_point": "Describing Properties of the Tangent Function",
    "problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=tan⁡x?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\n- The domain of the function is all real numbers except $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi $\n- The function has zeros at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi $ for any integer $n$\n- The range of the function is $y\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{\\pi }{4})$",
    "worked_solution": "Let's plot the graph of $y=tan⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933873/assets/732955302ca49a41f6c43cf242d7c869e630e88d804c4b56a5beb3b081f2d230.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true. The function is defined everywhere, except where $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .$\n\n- Statement II is false. The zeros occur at $x=0,\\pm \\pi ,\\pm 2\\pi ,…,$ which can be written as $x=n\\pi .$\n\n- Statement III is false. The function takes values on all the real numbers, hence the range is $y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I only\".",
